Relationship to mp3gain
-----------------------
Gain dB is a Python re-implementation that reproduces the behavior,
command-line option scheme, and the file and tag formats of mp3gain
(https://sourceforge.net/projects/mp3gain/) in order to remain
compatible with it.

Portions of Gain dB are based on, or adapted from, the mp3gain C
sources, which are licensed under the GNU LGPL v2.1 or later:

  mp3gain -- Copyright (C) 2001-2009 Glen Sawyer
             AAC support (C) 2004-2009 David Lasker, Altos Design, Inc.
             ReplayGainAnalysis (C) 2001-2009 David Robinson and
             Glen Sawyer; improvements by Frank Klemm and Marcel Mueller
             ID3v2 / APEv2 tag handling by the mp3gain contributors

In particular, the modules gaindb/id3.py, gaindb/tag.py,
gaindb/frame.py and gaindb/writer.py follow the structure of the
corresponding mp3gain sources (id3tag.c, apetag.c, mp3gain.c) and are
distributed as modified versions under the same LGPL terms. The
changes relative to the originals are: translation from C to Python,
restructuring into Python modules/dataclasses, removal of
platform-specific code, and integration with the Gain dB API. See the
per-file headers for details.

Other components
----------------
- Loudness analysis (gaindb/analysis.py) implements the publicly
  documented ReplayGain specification. Filter coefficient values are
  public standard numbers shared across independent implementations.

- ffmpeg is NOT bundled. It is invoked as an external process located
  on the user's PATH; users must install it separately.

- The graphical interface uses PySide6 (Qt for Python), which is
  licensed under the GNU LGPL v3. It is linked dynamically so that
  users may replace the Qt libraries. When distributing pre-built
  binaries, the LGPL v3 text and a usage notice are included.

- NumPy and SciPy are used under the BSD 3-Clause License. See
  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

